{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>He seals every man's hand</b> — Some say: at the side of every man." "<b>He seals</b> — That the rain prevents them from going out, so that every man knows his field's work. Others said: that HaShem seals in every man's hand the deeds he will do, and He mentioned this matter in this verse on account of the rain, as in the manner of \"if you obey, I will give the rain of your land\" (Deuteronomy 11:13-14). And what is near to me: that He speaks of the sower, for after the rain falls people sow, and HaShem seals in the hand of each and every one what will come of the seed."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {1 "Resolved המקום as HaShem per the divine-names rule; Ibn Ezra uses המקום (\"the Place\") as a standard reverent circumlocution for God. The embedded citation paraphrases Deuteronomy 11:13-14 rather than quoting exactly."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:51.369890449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}